Subject: Forward declared interface-package indexes at runtime

Applies to: RCR rosidl_core_generators 0.4.3-3.rcr.5, defs.bzl.

Observed failure: a consumer of an interface package's generated ament_index
can import its Python message classes but cannot introspect nested definitions.
For example, geometry_msgs is unknown to a consumer of nav_msgs/its index.
C++ and Python binding dependencies are forwarded, but index dependencies are not.

Rationale and scope: forward the already-declared interface dependencies to
the generated ament_index, using the same label mapping as language providers.
Preserve package ownership and existing targets; do not infer undeclared sources
or maintain another top-level dependency-package list.

Verification: dependency_indexes_test passes all three package/resource lookups
(one unittest case, 0.2 s). The collection Python consumer also resolves nested
geometry_msgs resources and imports native type support with Cyclone DDS.

Upstream: the selected published macro lacks this edge, inspected 2026-11-23.
No matching upstream association is recorded.
https://bazel.ros.org/modules/rosidl_core_generators/0.4.3-3.rcr.5/source.json

